---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import CertBadge from '../components/CertBadge.astro';
import CtaButton from '../components/CtaButton.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { certs, certStats } from '../data/certs';

const snCerts = certs.filter((c) => c.group === 'servicenow');
const aiCerts = certs.filter((c) => c.group === 'ai');
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Lukasz Szumilas is a ServiceNow developer and consultant, a Udemy teacher with 10,000+ students, and a specialist in governed AI on the ServiceNow platform.">
  <PageHeader eyebrow="About" title="Lukasz Szumilas">
    ServiceNow developer and consultant. Udemy teacher. Building toward governed AI on the
    ServiceNow platform.
  </PageHeader>

  <Section>
    <div class="page-body flow">
      <p>
        I'm a self-taught generalist who learned to build, market, sell, automate, write, and
        teach, mostly by refusing to outsource my own education. ServiceNow is where that
        curiosity turned into a career.
      </p>
      <p>
        For the last 4+ years I've delivered ServiceNow for banks and insurers: ITSM, Service
        Portal and Employee Center, CMDB and CSDM, and integrations in JavaScript and REST. The
        environments are demanding, and the work has to hold up to a security review. That
        shaped how I think about everything else, including AI.
      </p>
      <p>
        Alongside the consulting, I teach. Lucky X is my course brand on Udemy, with practice
        tests used by more than 10,000 students. It runs on one rule: I only build a course for
        an exam I've personally passed on the first attempt, and every explanation links back to
        official ServiceNow documentation so students learn the reasoning behind the answer.
        {' '}{certStats.total} certifications later, that rule hasn't changed.
      </p>
      <p>
        Now I'm pointing the same discipline at AI. The interesting work is governed AI on
        ServiceNow that a bank's security team will actually sign off on: MCP done right, with
        data that stays where it belongs and agents that do only what they're allowed to.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="surface">
    <p class="eyebrow">Credentials</p>
    <h2 class="section-h2 display">{certStats.total} certifications, {certStats.passedFirstTry}</h2>
    <h3 class="cert-group-title">ServiceNow</h3>
    <div class="cert-grid">
      {snCerts.map((c) => <CertBadge code={c.code} name={c.name} />)}
    </div>
    <h3 class="cert-group-title">AI</h3>
    <div class="cert-grid">
      {aiCerts.map((c) => <CertBadge code={c.code} name={c.name} />)}
    </div>
    <p class="muted cert-note">
      The list above is representative. The full set spans 17 ServiceNow certifications across
      administration, development, and implementation tracks.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section>
    <div class="two-col">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What I do</p>
        <ul class="do-list flow" role="list">
          <li><strong>Consulting.</strong> ServiceNow delivery plus governed AI for enterprise teams.</li>
          <li><strong>Teaching.</strong> Lucky X certification practice tests on Udemy.</li>
          <li><strong>Writing.</strong> ServiceNow, MCP, and AI on the platform, here and on LinkedIn.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Languages</p>
        <ul class="do-list flow" role="list">
          <li>Polish, native</li>
          <li>English, C2</li>
          <li>German, B1</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="cv-cta">
          <CtaButton href={site.socials.linkedin} variant="secondary" external>Full experience on LinkedIn</CtaButton>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="dark">
    <div class="cta-band">
      <h2 class="section-h2 display">Want to work together?</h2>
      <div class="cluster">
        <CtaButton href="/consulting/">Work with me</CtaButton>
        <CtaButton href="/newsletter/" variant="secondary">Get the newsletter</CtaButton>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-body {
    max-width: var(--maxw-prose);
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .section-h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
  .cert-group-title {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0.85rem;
  }
  .cert-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 15rem), 1fr));
  }
  .cert-note {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    max-width: 60ch;
  }
  .two-col {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
  .do-list {
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .do-list li {
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .cv-cta {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .cta-band {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }
  @media (min-width: 720px) {
    .two-col {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
